# COPILOT PROMPT — Build CodeGraph as a VS Code VSIX Extension

## MISSION

Build a production-ready VS Code extension (`.vsix`) called **CodeGraph** that replicates every capability of `colbymchenry/codegraph` — but instead of an MCP server, it exposes all intelligence directly inside VS Code via commands, a sidebar panel, CodeLens, hover providers, and an inline chat participant. Zero MCP. Zero external servers. Zero pre-requisites. 100% local SQLite graph (sql.js WASM — no native binaries), tree-sitter ASTs (web-tree-sitter WASM), native VS Code file watching. The VSIX must install and run on Windows, macOS, and Linux with a single double-click — no Node.js, no npm, no compiler toolchain required on the end user's machine.

