## HARD RULES

- Python: 4-space indentation. JS/TS: 2-space indentation.
- Zero placeholders. Every method body is fully implemented.
- Zero `any` types unless interfacing with raw tree-sitter SyntaxNode.
- No markdown file generation unless the user asks.
- Flat, linear logic. No deep abstractions. Simple is correct.
- `sql.js` (WASM SQLite) for all DB access — zero native binaries, works on all platforms out of the box. Persist via `db.export()` after every batch write. Initialize from `wasm/sql-wasm.wasm` via `locateFile`.
- All tree-sitter grammars loaded from `context.asAbsolutePath('grammars/')`.
- All WASM grammar `.wasm` files copied to `grammars/` directory at build time via a script.
- The extension must work offline. No network calls of any kind.
- `.codegraph/` directory and `codegraph.db` file created automatically on first index.
- Incremental indexing: files whose content hash is unchanged are skipped — never re-parsed.
